{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Lo hear my counsel fair and true for thy voyage to the fair isle of Japan.\n\nFirst upon the morrow of thine arrival come forth to the bustling streets of Tokyo. There shalt thou wander through the neon-lit bazaars of Shibuya and behold the towering edifice of Tokyo Skytree. In the eve repair to a traditional ryokan where thou shalt sup upon delicacies most fine and rest thy weary bones.\n\nOn the second day take carriage to the ancient capital of Kyoto. Walk in the gardens of the Imperial Palace and marvel at the vermilion torii gates of Fushimi Inari. Pay homage to the spirits in the temples of Kinkaku-ji and Kiyomizu-dera. As the sun doth set partake in a tea ceremony most reverent.\n\nThe third morn embark upon the Tokaido Shinkansen to the city of Osaka. There feast upon takoyaki and okonomiyaki in Dotonbori and gaze upon the mighty Osaka Castle. In the gloaming take a river cruise upon the Okawa and drink in the sights and sounds of the city.\n\nOn the fourth day venture to Hiroshima. Pay thy respects at the Peace Memorial Park and Museum. In the eve journey to the isle of Miyajima and witness the floating torii gate of Itsukushima Shrine as the tide doth rise.\n\nThe fifth day return to Kyoto for a final night of reflection and rest ere thy departure on the morrow.\n\nFare thee well on thy journey and may the gods of old smile upon thy travels.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Lo", "logprob": -3.17645525932312}, {"token": " hear", "logprob": -4.379876136779785}, {"token": " my", "logprob": -1.7547938823699951}, {"token": " counsel", "logprob": -0.4834710359573364}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.4973583221435547}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.34768858551979065}, {"token": " true", "logprob": -0.2658693492412567}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.21008767187595367}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -0.11420821398496628}, {"token": " voyage", "l